---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this blog">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">About</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg">
      <p>
        Welcome to this simple, modern tech blog built with <strong>Astro</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is pure simplicity:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Write posts in Markdown</li>
        <li>Push to GitHub</li>
        <li>Vercel or Netlify automatically deploys</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Perfect for AI-assisted content creation. Just generate a Markdown file with the right frontmatter and commit it.
      </p>
      <h2>How AI can write posts</h2>
      <p>
        Give any AI this format and ask it to create a new file in <code>src/content/blog/</code>:
      </p>
    </div>

    <pre class="mt-6 bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-5 rounded-xl overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>---
title: "Your Post Title"
description: "A short description for SEO and cards"
pubDate: 2026-09-16
tags: ["astro", "blog", "ai"]
heroImage: "/images/optional-image.jpg"
---

Your markdown content goes here...</code></pre>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
